course: dictionary
lesson: 2259
title: Crazy: many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Crazy has more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. Its main meaning is very silly, wild or strange: a crazy idea is not a sensible idea.
explain: The words next to crazy change its meaning. «Crazy about» football means you like football very much. In «crazy busy», crazy means very, so the day was very busy.
explain: Look at the feeling in the sentence too. «You're driving me round the bend» means you are making me very annoyed, so crazy means mad with annoyance here. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Crazy means very silly, wild or strange.
fact: «Crazy about» something means liking it very much.
fact: People also say crazy to mean very, as in «crazy busy».
fact: Long ago, crazy meant mentally ill. We do not use it that way today, because it can hurt people.
fact: On a crazy hair day at school, children wear wild, silly hair for fun.
exercise: Ella wore «crazy socks» on sock day. What does crazy mean here? | Very old | Very quiet and calm | *Very silly and bright | Very cold and wet
exercise: Sam says, «I am crazy about dinosaurs.» What does crazy mean? | He is scared of dinosaurs | He has never seen a dinosaur | He is angry with dinosaurs | *He likes dinosaurs very much
exercise: «The traffic was crazy busy.» What does crazy mean here? | Silly and wild | *Very busy | Grey and wet | Mentally ill
test: «It's enough to drive one crazy!» What does crazy mean here? | *Very annoying, making you cross | Very hungry | Very quiet and calm | Very kind and gentle
test: Lily says, «That is a crazy idea!» What does crazy mean in this sentence? | Very tired | Very old | *Very silly or wild | Very wet
exam: Why might a careful writer avoid using crazy to mean mentally ill? | It means happy and calm | It is a word for food | *It can hurt people who are ill | It is too long to read
